[Applause]  give me one minute and i'll show you how  beyond corp enterprise can secure access  to your services from beyond the  corporate walls  companies are increasingly more  distributed as employees work in more  locations  connecting to a vpn can be slow for  employees located far away from the  headquarters  however granting flat access to internal  apps based only on the network can also  be dangerous with a network-centric  model attackers can exfiltrate data just  by gaining access to the network to  solve these problems beyond corp  enterprise pushes security checks from  the network back to the user's device  and context  it does this by creating a proxy in  front of apps running in gcp other cloud  platforms or on-premises  the proxy passes through or blocks  traffic based on the requester's device  information their identity and hundreds  of other signals  for example you can choose to allow  access to hr apps only for devices  managed by the company for added  security you can enforce multi-factor  authentication as well  to secure hr apps using access context  manager define an access level  this level includes requests from  devices managed by the company and  requests authenticated with multi-factor  next using identity aware proxy map the  new access level to the hr web app  so next time you're looking to shift to  a zero trust context-diverse security  model take a minute to look at beyond  forb enterprise  to learn more check out cloud.google.com  beyondcorp enterprise

